# The restoration package's own documents, tests and data are kept byte for byte (its checksum list names them), so no line-ending
# normalisation and no text conversion whatever core.autocrlf says.
docs/development/package/** -text

# The author's release and his source are kept byte for byte: the ROM is compared with its SHA-256, and the source is assembled by the tests into
# exactly that ROM (the assembler reads lines, but the .incbin files, the character sheet and the compressed pictures are binary).
reference/** -text
reference/release/Lan_Master.nes binary
reference/source/*.rle binary
reference/source/*.chr binary
reference/source/*.bin binary

*.png binary
